From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 06:08:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse owned-array base object allocations

Cache a small number of destroyed PySliceContainer allocations on
GIL-enabled builds. The Rust buffer destructor still runs before the shell
is retained, and every subsequent initializer supplies a new pointer,
length, capacity and destructor.

Use PyO3's backend selection so free-threaded-compatible builds retain
their native allocation path.
---
diff --git a/src/slice_container.rs b/src/slice_container.rs
index 991dbe931..bb57b6cce 100644
--- a/src/slice_container.rs
+++ b/src/slice_container.rs
@@ -2,11 +2,11 @@ use std::{mem, ptr};
 
 use ndarray::{ArrayBase, Dimension, OwnedRepr};
 use pyo3::pyclass;
 
 /// Utility type to safely store `Box<[_]>` or `Vec<_>` on the Python heap
-#[pyclass(frozen)]
+#[pyclass(frozen, freelist = 8)]
 #[derive(Debug)]
 pub(crate) struct PySliceContainer {
     pub(crate) ptr: *mut u8,
     pub(crate) len: usize,
     cap: usize,
